spec
goal: evaluate every configured feature flag deterministically without mutating inputs

scope:
  edit: solution.py
  contract: evaluate_flags(user, flags) -> {flag_key:boolean}

rules:
  R1: return one entry per flag in input order; a flag is off unless enabled is exactly true
  R2: depends_on must resolve true for the same user; missing dependency -> false
  R3: every flag in a dependency cycle and every flag depending on that cycle -> false
  R4: present allow_users/countries/plans are AND gates against user["id"], user["country"], user["plan"]; absent user value, empty list, or nonmatch -> false
  R5: rollout defaults to 100; 0 -> false; 100 -> true after R1-R4
  R6: for rollout 1..99, hash UTF-8 "<user id>:<flag key>" with SHA-256, parse first 8 hex chars as base-16 integer, bucket modulo 100; true iff bucket<rollout
  R7: use no randomness, clock, or network; preserve user, flags, and nested lists

acceptance:
  A1: R1,R4-R7 cover enabled state, targeting, allowlists, and rollout
  A2: R2,R3 cover dependency chains, missing dependencies, cycles, and cycle dependents
